{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>From the wilderness of Kedemot.</b> Even though the Omnipresent did not command me to call to Sihon for peace, I learned it from the wilderness of Sinai — from the Torah that preceded the world: when the Holy One, blessed be He, came to give it to Israel, He first offered it to Esau and Ishmael, and it was known before Him that they would not accept it, and even so He opened to them with peace — so I too preceded Sihon with words of peace. Another interpretation: <b>from the wilderness of Kedemot</b> — 'From You I learned,' that You preceded the world: You could have sent one bolt of lightning and consumed the Egyptians, but You sent me from the wilderness to Pharaoh to say (Exodus 5) ״Send My people,״ with gentleness (Tanchuma)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:45:43.342826133Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}